&lt;h3&gt;


1. Shadcn/ui - Best free component library
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Shadcn/ui is genuinely the best free alternative to Tailwind UI for component quality. It ships Button, Input, Select, Dialog, Table, Tabs, and 40+ other components that are well-designed, accessible, and work natively with Next.js App Router and Tailwind CSS. You copy-paste components into your project (they become your code, not a dependency), which means full flexibility to modify them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free and open source - MIT license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;40+ high-quality components including data table, command, and combobox&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native Next.js App Router support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dark mode supported via CSS variables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active development - new components added regularly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Components only - you build the full page layouts yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Radix UI - Best free headless component library
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Radix UI provides the accessible, unstyled primitives that Shadcn/ui is built on. If you want maximum styling control and are comfortable writing all your own CSS, Radix gives you correct keyboard navigation, ARIA attributes, and focus management without any visual opinions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free and open source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WAI-ARIA compliant out of the box&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No styles - bring your own CSS or Tailwind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Used internally by Shadcn/ui and many other component systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires more setup than Shadcn/ui&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Headless UI - Best free Tailwind-native components
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Headless UI is made by the same team as Tailwind CSS and Tailwind Plus. It provides unstyled accessible components (Dialog, Listbox, Combobox, Menu, Tabs) designed specifically to be styled with Tailwind CSS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free and open source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Made by Tailwind Labs - best Tailwind CSS integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Covers the tricky interactive components (dropdown, combobox, dialog)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Smaller set than Shadcn/ui - 10 components vs 40+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React and Vue versions available&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When you need a template, not components
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All three free options above are component libraries - they give you building blocks, not pages. If your goal is to ship a complete product quickly (a SaaS landing page, dashboard, portfolio, or agency site), you'll spend 1-3 weeks assembling components into full page layouts before you have something shippable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TheKitBase is not a free alternative - it starts at $39. But it is a complete template alternative to Tailwind Plus, not just a component alternative. You get 7-11 fully designed pages you can customize and ship in hours, not weeks.&lt;/p&gt;

